
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy, Unfortunately";
}

<div class="privacy-page">

    <div class="privacy-hero">
        <div class="privacy-hero-content">
            <span class="privacy-eyebrow">THE LITTLE LIBRARY / LEGAL DEPARTMENT (UNPAID)</span>
            <h1>Your secrets are<br />safe-ish. Probably.</h1>
            <p>
                Welcome to our Privacy Policy, the page everyone ignores
                until a website asks for their email and suddenly becomes suspicious.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="privacy-hero-art">
            <div class="privacy-lock">🔒</div>
            <span>TRUST ISSUES: ENABLED</span>
            <small>Protected by vibes and several lines of code.</small>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="privacy-intro">
        <div>
            <span class="privacy-section-label">THE SHORT VERSION (FINALLY)</span>
            <h2>We collect data, not your soul.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
            This is a school library project. We're trying to manage books and
            members, not build a criminal investigation board about your life.
            Please calm down, Google.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="privacy-grid">

        <article class="privacy-card">
            <span class="privacy-number">01 / THE NOSY PART</span>
            <div class="privacy-card-icon">📋</div>
            <h3>What we collect</h3>
            <p>
                Your name, email, and membership details may be recorded
                so the library knows who you are. Revolutionary technology,
                we know.
            </p>
            <p class="privacy-joke">
                We don't need your birth chart, your search history, or the
                name of the person who left you on read.
            </p>
        </article>

        <article class="privacy-card">
            <span class="privacy-number">02 / OUR GRAND PLAN</span>
            <div class="privacy-card-icon">📚</div>
            <h3>What we do with it</h3>
            <p>
                We use your information to manage library records, organize
                memberships, and make this project look like we knew what
                we were doing all along.
            </p>
            <p class="privacy-joke">
                No evil master plan. We can barely finish the normal plan.
            </p>
        </article>

        <article class="privacy-card">
            <span class="privacy-number">03 / PLEASE DON'T HACK US</span>
            <div class="privacy-card-icon">🛡️</div>
            <h3>Keeping it safe</h3>
            <p>
                We aim to handle stored information responsibly. Security
                matters, even if our computer sounds like it's preparing
                for takeoff every time we open Visual Studio.
            </p>
            <p class="privacy-joke">
                If the laptop starts speaking binary, we're calling the
                instructor. That's above our pay grade.
            </p>
        </article>

        <article class="privacy-card">
            <span class="privacy-number">04 / THE GOSSIP DEPARTMENT</span>
            <div class="privacy-card-icon">👀</div>
            <h3>Who can see it?</h3>
            <p>
                Member information should only be accessed by people who
                need it for library-related tasks. Your data isn't public
                entertainment. We have enough problems already.
            </p>
            <p class="privacy-joke">
                Nobody is hosting a PowerPoint presentation about your
                membership type. We hope.
            </p>
        </article>

        <article class="privacy-card">
            <span class="privacy-number">05 / YOU HAVE RIGHTS, BESTIE</span>
            <div class="privacy-card-icon">✉️</div>
            <h3>You have a say</h3>
            <p>
                You may be able to request access to or correction of your
                personal information, depending on applicable privacy rules.
                Basically, speak up if something looks wrong.
            </p>
            <p class="privacy-joke">
                We accept questions, corrections, and constructive criticism.
                Unsolicited code reviews may cause emotional damage.
            </p>
        </article>

        <article class="privacy-card">
            <span class="privacy-number">06 / PLOT TWIST</span>
            <div class="privacy-card-icon">🔄</div>
            <h3>Things may change</h3>
            <p>
                This page may change as the website develops. New features,
                new requirements, new bugs. The circle of student life.
            </p>
            <p class="privacy-joke">
                If the wording changes overnight, either we improved it
                or something broke. Both are equally possible.
            </p>
        </article>

    </div>

    <div class="privacy-disclaimer">
        <div class="privacy-disclaimer-icon">⚠️</div>
        <div>
            <h3>One serious thing. Don't get used to it.</h3>
            <p>
                This is a school project, not a legally reviewed privacy
                policy. The actual data practices depend on how the website
                is built and used. Please don't treat the jokes as a security
                guarantee. Our code has enough pressure already.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="privacy-bottom">
        <span>THE LITTLE LIBRARY</span>
        <span>Read books. Protect data. Submit before the deadline.</span>
    </div>

</div>
